\node at (5.1,3) {$B$};
\node at (1.9,2) {$8$};
\node at (3.5,2) {$4$};
\node at (5.1,2) {$6$};
\node at (6.4,0.5) {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Describe the reduced sample space for $P(A\mid B)$ and calculate this probability.
b. Find $P(B\mid A)$.
c. Find $P(A\mid B')$.

workedExamples.solution_text:
a. Knowing that $B$ occurred excludes everything outside $B$. The reduced sample space contains $4+6=10$ outcomes; $4$ also belong to $A$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conditionfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\definecolor{overlapfill}{HTML}{E8DEF4}
\fill[conditionfill] (4.4,2) circle (1.5);
\begin{scope}
\clip (2.6,2) circle (1.5);
\fill[overlapfill] (4.4,2) circle (1.5);
\end{scope}
\draw (0,0) rectangle (7,4);
\draw (2.6,2) circle (1.5);
\draw[thick] (4.4,2) circle (1.5);
\node at (1.9,3) {$A$};
\node at (5.1,3) {$B$};
\node at (1.9,2) {$8$};
\node at (3.5,2) {$4$};
\node at (5.1,2) {$6$};
\node at (6.4,0.5) {$2$};
\node[anchor=north] at (3.5,-0.15) {Blue and purple: condition $B$; purple: favourable overlap};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}P(A\mid B)&=\frac{n(A\cap B)}{n(B)}\\&=\frac{4}{10}\\&=\frac{2}{5}\end{aligned}$

b. The condition is now $A$, containing $8+4=12$ outcomes.
$\begin{aligned}P(B\mid A)&=\frac{4}{12}\\&=\frac{1}{3}\end{aligned}$
Swapping the event and condition changes the denominator.

c. The condition $B'$ includes the $8$ outcomes in $A$ only and the $2$ outside both circles. Only the $8$ in $A$ are favourable.
$\begin{aligned}P(A\mid B')&=\frac{8}{8+2}\\&=\frac{4}{5}\end{aligned}$

